silo install: project silo-test-project

  prereqs           ok      credentials ok; billing on; CPUS us-central1 2/24 used; NETWORKS 1/15;
                            firewall policy rule attributes 2000 (not reported by Cloud Quotas: the
                            documented default), for about 360 silos; no organization
  apis              ok      11 APIs enabled
  db-instance       update  silo-db-t3st tier db-g1-small, not db-f1-micro; public IP false, not
                            true; cloudsql.iam_authentication on, not off; maintenance window
                            sun:05:00, not mon:05:00 (restarts the instance)
  service-account   update  silod@silo-test-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com display name and
                            description
                            silod@silo-test-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com enable: it is disabled
  role              update  projects/silo-test-project/roles/silod permissions
                            +compute.instances.create, -iam.roles.create
                    create  roles/logging.logWriter bound to silod
  network           ok      silo
  gateway-subnet    update  silo-gateway Private Google Access on
  control-subnet    update  silo-ctl Private Google Access off
  nat               update  silo-gateway-nat for silo-gateway only, with automatic addresses
  fence             update  silo-fence patch catch-out at 2147483001
                    create  silo-fence -> silo association
  address           ok      silo-gateway-ip 10.255.255.2
  dns               update  silo-internal visible to silo
                            silo.internal. A 10.255.255.2, not 10.9.9.9
  image             ok      silo silod@sha256:7dd5524d6d0b
  db                ok      database silo, IAM user silod@silo-test-project.iam
  db-endpoint       update  silo-db visible to silo, t3st.us-central1.sql.goog. A 10.255.254.2
  migrate           ok      schema 17
  control           ok      silo-control us-central1-a, silod@sha256:7dd5524d6d0b
  root              ok      / exists (changed through the fence API, not by install)
  admin             create  user:admin@example.com roles/iap.tunnelResourceAccessor on silo-control
  verify            ok      / regions us-central1, europe-west4; blocks 10.0.0.0/8; europe-west4
                            vcpu 24, ssd_disk_gb 500, local_ssd_gb 0; us-central1 vcpu 22,
                            ssd_disk_gb 500, local_ssd_gb 0

  20 steps: 1 to create or apply, 9 to update, 10 ok
  Estimated time: about 7 minutes, most of it waiting for Cloud SQL.
